          "npc": true,
          "name": "Shopkeeper Oswin",
          "tint": [
            1,
            0.9,
            0.6
          ],
          "text": "Blades, mail, charms and sigils, all honestly priced. And your company's kit can be sorted out right here at the counter.",
          "rune_service": true,
          "dialogue": [
            "Oswin rubs a thumb over a scar in the counter. 'A rune is not a bauble. It remembers every hand that has carried it.'",
            "'I can seat a rune safely, or draw one out without cracking the socket. A field swap is how good steel gets ruined.'",
            "'Bring me three of the same mark for the Forge. Their grades need not match, but a well-trained rune gives the ritual a steadier chance.'"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
