          "kind": "text",
          "npc": true,
          "name": "Steward Brannoch",
          "tint": [
            0.95,
            0.8,
            0.5
          ],
          "text": "The road is open, my lord, but it is not safe. Train the company, forge sigils, and clear the Roadwolf Camp.",
          "dialogue": [
            "'Your house held this valley by oath, not by walls. Walls can be raised again; trust takes longer.'",
            "'The quartermaster has sent word of a smith at the lower gate. He can temper any weapon or piece of armor to +15, though the price rises with every strike.'",
            "'The old families kept heirloom runes apart from common stock. They are not merchandise. They choose their bearer.'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "cell": [
            7,
            4
          ],
          "kind": "party",
          "npc": false,
          "name": "War Table",
          "text": "The war table: sort your company, gear, sigils and promotions here, or send for the market stock.",
          "dialogue": [
            "'Scouts have marked three approaches: river, ridge and forest. Each battlefield will answer differently to the ground beneath your boots.'",
            "'Take the high ground where you can. A narrow ford is a fine place to hold a line, and a poor place to retreat.'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "cell": [
            4,
            8
          ],
          "kind": "party",
          "npc": true,
          "name": "Master Smith Rurik",
          "tint": [
            0.9,
            0.65,
            0.35
          ],
          "text": "Rurik's arms are black with forge soot. He measures every blade as if it were a promise.",
          "dialogue": [
            "'Steel has a memory. Every temper leaves a little of the smith in it.'",
            "'I can improve a weapon or armor to +15. I can also draw socketed runes without damaging them. Nothing is free but advice.'"
          ],
          "blacksmith": true,
          "rune_service": true,
          "shopkeeper_id": "rurik"
        }
      ]
    },
